  "term": "behavior checklist",
  "definition": "A behavior checklist is an assessment tool used to gather information about an adult’s behaviors and problems from the person and from others who know them well. It can be used in settings such as counseling, mental health, medical, forensic, and substance use services, and summarizes results on problem-related scales.",
